{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Government to commit to stability for UK work and graduate visa rules",
        "additional_details": "We believe migrant workers & businesses are vital drivers of the UK economy. HMRC records show immigrants pay over \u00a320bn annually in direct taxes, with non-EU migrants yielding a \u00a34.6bn net surplus. Immigrants own 27% of UK businesses, creating over 1.1 million jobs. Home Office accounts also show \u00a323.19bn was extracted via visa fees and levies (2019-25). We believe abrupt visa rule changes can create severe anxiety & damage talent retention.",
        "background": "We want the UK Government to commit to a stable, long-term immigration framework and halt sudden, restrictive shifts to salary thresholds, visa durations, and settlement paths.",
